From 651cc607c7fc10926beba02401856db68f456612 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:06:56 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wallet(v2): write a legacy keypool top-up in one SQLite
 transaction

Creating an encrypted legacy wallet with the default 1000-key keypool
took about 38 seconds on regtest here (3.5 minutes reported elsewhere),
against about 1.5 seconds for the same RPC on Bitcoin ABC. A profile of
createwallet shows almost all of the time in fcntl(F_FULLFSYNC) under
sqlite3_step, called from LegacyScriptPubKeyMan::TopUp: neither
encryption nor key derivation is significant.

TopUp writes several records per key (the key or crypted key, its
metadata, the HD chain counter and the pool entry), 2000 keys in all.
Berkeley DB buffered these writes in its environment log. Since v2/033
moved legacy wallets to SQLite, each write runs outside a transaction,
so SQLite commits it durably on its own, with several full fsyncs per
commit. The encrypted path issues the most writes; an unencrypted
wallet was slow too (about 9 seconds).

TopUp now writes the new keys in one transaction, and NewKeyPool wraps
erasing the old pool and the top-up in one. When a transaction is
already open (EncryptWallet), the writes join it. A failed commit
throws, as a failed write already did. Encryption is unchanged: every
key is still encrypted with the master key, and the passphrase
derivation is still calibrated to about 100 ms.

createwallet with a passphrase now takes about 1 second, and without
one about 0.4 seconds. The keypool and keys survive a restart, and the
wallet unlocks and dumps a key from the restored pool.

Tier: V2 (fixup to v2/033)
---
 src/wallet/scriptpubkeyman.cpp | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/wallet/scriptpubkeyman.cpp b/src/wallet/scriptpubkeyman.cpp
index b000ebbee7..3d596a11c3 100644
--- a/src/wallet/scriptpubkeyman.cpp
+++ b/src/wallet/scriptpubkeyman.cpp
@@ -1195,6 +1195,10 @@ bool LegacyScriptPubKeyMan::NewKeyPool() {
     }
     LOCK(cs_KeyStore);
     WalletBatch batch(m_storage.GetDatabase());
+    // Erase the old pool and write the new one in one database transaction
+    // (see TopUp). Returns false if a transaction is already open; its owner
+    // then commits these writes.
+    const bool own_txn = batch.TxnBegin();
 
     for (const int64_t nIndex : setInternalKeyPool) {
         batch.ErasePool(nIndex);
@@ -1214,8 +1218,15 @@ bool LegacyScriptPubKeyMan::NewKeyPool() {
     m_pool_key_to_index.clear();
 
     if (!TopUp()) {
+        if (own_txn) {
+            batch.TxnAbort();
+        }
         return false;
     }
+    if (own_txn && !batch.TxnCommit()) {
+        throw std::runtime_error(std::string(__func__) +
+                                 ": committing the new keypool failed");
+    }
 
     WalletLogPrintf("LegacyScriptPubKeyMan::NewKeyPool rewrote keypool\n");
     return true;
@@ -1255,6 +1266,14 @@ bool LegacyScriptPubKeyMan::TopUp(unsigned int kpSize) {
         }
         bool internal = false;
         WalletBatch batch(m_storage.GetDatabase());
+        // Each new key takes several writes (key, metadata, HD chain, pool
+        // entry). On SQLite every write outside a transaction is its own
+        // durable commit with several (full) fsyncs, which made a default
+        // 2000-key top-up take minutes. Write them all in one transaction.
+        // If one is already open (NewKeyPool, EncryptWallet), these writes
+        // join it and its owner commits them.
+        const bool own_txn =
+            missingInternal + missingExternal > 0 && batch.TxnBegin();
         for (int64_t i = missingInternal + missingExternal; i--;) {
             if (i < missingInternal) {
                 internal = true;
@@ -1263,6 +1282,10 @@ bool LegacyScriptPubKeyMan::TopUp(unsigned int kpSize) {
             CPubKey pubkey(GenerateNewKey(batch, m_hd_chain, internal));
             AddKeypoolPubkeyWithDB(pubkey, internal, batch);
         }
+        if (own_txn && !batch.TxnCommit()) {
+            throw std::runtime_error(std::string(__func__) +
+                                     ": committing new keypool keys failed");
+        }
         if (missingInternal + missingExternal > 0) {
             WalletLogPrintf(
                 "keypool added %d keys (%d internal), size=%u (%u internal)\n",
-- 
